# Hofund conventions

This rule restates [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Follow it on every change.

## Language

Write standard English only: code, identifiers, comments, docs, commit
messages, pull request titles and descriptions, issue text, CI names, and
error messages.

The only exceptions are future i18n language-pack files and translated
READMEs named `README.<lang>.md`. `README.md` is always English. Do not mix
languages inside a source file.

## Architecture

Spine, dependencies point downward only:

`ir ← codec ← provider ← router ← gateway ← daemon ← cli`

- `agent` depends only on `config`, never on `gateway`.
- Vendor names must never appear in `crates/gateway` or `crates/router`.
  Quirks live in `quirks` data and provider adapters. Protocol names belong
  in `codec`.
- Only `gateway` may depend on axum, tower, or hyper.
- No runtime crate depends on `xtask`.
- Do not create `apps/desktop` unless the task asks. It is reserved for a
  future Tauri v2 menu-bar app.
- Do not use the magpie name or logo as hofund branding. Credit stays in
  `README.md`, `README.zh-CN.md`, and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

The dependency table in `docs/architecture.md` and `expected_deps` in
`xtask/tests/workspace_invariants.rs` are normative. Update both, plus the
manifest, when an edge changes.

## Learning from the upstream project

Before building a subsystem, study how yetone/magpie does that part. Adopt
behavior that is sound, stable, and efficient, reimplemented in idiomatic
Rust. Do not copy its source; keep the MIT notice in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
Redesign what is unsound: small types, trait boundaries, explicit constructor
state, no globals, testable units. Record each choice in
`docs/magpie-comparison.md` and update that table when the subsystem changes.
Do not use that project's name as hofund branding.

## Verify

Pinned toolchain: Rust 1.99.1, edition 2024. `unsafe` is forbidden.

```sh
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace
```

This tree is a pre-alpha scaffold. Do not add product behavior unless the
task asks for it.
